sues succeeds and the guard raises afterward), and the four re-raise sites are bare `raise` — so either accept that the exception message is the sole signal or have `_paged_search` log a WARNING immediately before raising `BackendPaginationStallError`.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan step 4: 'the propagated error aborts the pass with the transport's own _call_logged WARNING already emitted (_base.py:60-66) plus the raised message — instrumented, not an uninstrumented traceback.'","_base.py:61-67: _call_logged wraps only `return _with_connection_retry(fn, ...)` in try/except and logs the WARNING solely inside `except Exception: ...; raise` — i.e. only when fn() fails.","On a stall fn() (search_issues) returns a non-empty repeated batch successfully; the guard raises BackendPaginationStallError at the pager level, outside _call_logged's try — so no _call_logged WARNING is produced.","The re-raise sites cited in the plan are bare `raise` with no logging (verified _hierarchy.py re-raise clause and fetcher.py's three `except BackendPaginationStallError: raise` clauses)."],"finding":"Step 4's instrumentation rationale is factually incorrect: it claims the propagated stall aborts the pass 'with the transport's own _call_logged WARNING already emitted (_base.py:60-66) plus the raised message — instrumented, not an uninstrumented traceback,' but _call_logged only emits its WARNING when the wrapped search_issues call itself raises. On a stall, search_issues SUCCEEDS (returns the repeated page) and BackendPaginationStallError is raised by the pager logic AFTER _call_logged returns, so that WARNING never fires on the stall path. The get_parent_map and three fetcher re-raise sites are bare `raise` with no log, so the only signal on the stall path is the exception message.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f97036cd6b9dc463b","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section 'Plan', step 4 (fetcher.py re-raise rationale)","norm_id":"n8e7bc9ac0a3b8689","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","scenarios":["An offset-blind DC instance triggers the stall in production; an operator inspecting logs to understand why the pass aborted finds only the raised exception, not the WARNING the plan promised at the transport boundary."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"In _paged_search, emit `logger.warning(...)` naming the stalled startAt/JQL immediately before `raise BackendPaginationStallError(...)`, and update the plan text to stop attributing the signal to _call_logged (which only fires when the wrapped call raises, not on a successful repeated page).","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v4","material_fingerprint":"1aa8b9642d6e70a5","metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":1345450,"cache_write_tokens":295918,"claim_path":"no-llm/no-network (structural; the fast claim check is a local HMAC verify)","det_ms":534.8,"input_tokens":1658257,"llm_calls":30,"llm_ms":158730.0,"output_tokens":33757,"total_ms":160604.3,"verify_requests":7},"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","p